  "raw": "\n\nI had a friend of mine tell me about my first blog post, so I thought I'd come back and do one now. I have the same kind of question for all WP's, however; if they want to discuss that question, they can do it here.\n\nI want quality in my responses. I'm not interested in what you think of my blog's design or whatever. I'm not interested in writing a post just to get \"likes.\" I'm not interested in spam. But at the same time, that doesn't mean I don't like it when someone is being helpful to people. So in that way I consider myself a \"non-spammy (and non-self-centered) WP.\" But if you have a great idea or an interesting question, a quality post on your own blog, or something to share about the WP you'd like to discuss, that's all good.\n\nAhem. Now I need a drink.\n\n",
  "serialized": "I had a friend of mine tell me about my first blog post, so I thought I'd come back and do one now. I have the same kind of question for all WP's, however; if they want to discuss that question, they can do it here. I want quality in my responses. I'm not interested in what you think of my blog's design or whatever. I'm not interested in writing a post just to get \"likes.\" I'm not interested in spam. But at the same time, that doesn't mean I don't like it when someone is being helpful to people. So in that way I consider myself a \"non-spammy (and non-self-centered) WP.\" But if you have a great idea or an interesting question, a quality post on your own blog, or something to share about the WP you'd like to discuss, that's all good. Ahem. Now I need a drink.",
